---
// Civil Structural & Hauling Logistics Block
---
<section class="civil-block-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="civil-card">
      <div class="civil-header">
        <div class="civil-icon">
          <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8">
            <rect x="1" y="3" width="15" height="13"></rect>
            <polygon points="16 8 20 8 23 11 23 16 16 16 16 8"></polygon>
            <circle cx="5.5" cy="18.5" r="2.5"></circle>
            <circle cx="18.5" cy="18.5" r="2.5"></circle>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="civil-badge">Commercial Logistics</span>
          <h3>Quarry Hauling Capacities & Truckload Planning</h3>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="civil-intro">
        Civil and heavy driveway aggregates are priced and hauled based on commercial truck payload limits. Standard haul rates incur drop fees ($65–$120+); ordering full truckload increments minimizes ton-mile freight costs:
      </p>

      <div class="truck-grid">
        <div class="truck-item">
          <div class="truck-name">Single-Axle Dump</div>
          <div class="truck-capacity">5 – 7 Tons</div>
          <div class="truck-yards">~3.5 to 5.0 yd³</div>
          <p class="truck-desc">Residential alleyways, tight driveways, and light utility repair drops.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="truck-item highlight">
          <div class="truck-badge-tag">Most Common</div>
          <div class="truck-name">Tandem-Axle Dump</div>
          <div class="truck-capacity">14 – 16 Tons</div>
          <div class="truck-yards">~10.0 to 11.5 yd³</div>
          <p class="truck-desc">Standard residential driveway delivery, slab sub-bases, and pole barn pads.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="truck-item">
          <div class="truck-name">Tri-Axle / Quad-Axle</div>
          <div class="truck-capacity">20 – 22 Tons</div>
          <div class="truck-yards">~14.0 to 15.5 yd³</div>
          <p class="truck-desc">Commercial parking pads, agricultural access lanes, and long rural drives.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="truck-item">
          <div class="truck-name">Semi End-Dump</div>
          <div class="truck-capacity">24 – 28 Tons</div>
          <div class="truck-yards">~17.0 to 19.5 yd³</div>
          <p class="truck-desc">Subdivision civil roads, large commercial site pads, and heavy highway base.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="subgrade-callout">
        <div class="subgrade-icon">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Geotechnical Stabilization Rule:</strong> For vehicular driveways over clay or soft loam, always lay <strong>woven subgrade geotextile fabric (Class 1 or 2)</strong> before spreading base aggregate. Woven fabric distributes wheel loads (CBR stabilization) and prevents the rock from sinking into the subgrade mud under heavy truck traffic.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .civil-block-section {
    padding: var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .civil-card {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.25);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    position: relative;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
  }

  .civil-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .civil-icon {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.15);
    border: 1px solid rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.3);
    color: #60a5fa;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .civil-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: #60a5fa;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }

  .civil-header h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .civil-intro {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .truck-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .truck-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .truck-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .truck-item {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .truck-item:hover {
    border-color: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.4);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .truck-item.highlight {
    border-color: rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.5);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.08) 0%, var(--bg-surface) 100%);
  }

  .truck-badge-tag {
    position: absolute;
    top: -10px;
    right: 12px;
    background: #2563eb;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .truck-name {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .truck-capacity {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #60a5fa;
  }

  .truck-yards {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .truck-desc {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .subgrade-callout {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    background: rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .subgrade-icon {
    color: #60a5fa;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .subgrade-callout strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
</style>
